.TH PACKROM 1 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 Development Tools"
.SH NAME
packrom \- pack a program, textures and sounds into a Vircon32 cartridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B packrom
.RB [ \-o
.IR output.v32 ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I definition.xml
.br
.B packrom
.B \-\-help
.br
.B packrom
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B packrom
reads a ROM definition \(em an XML file naming a program binary, its
textures and its sounds \(em and writes them as a single Vircon32 ROM
file: a cartridge
.RI ( .v32 )
that any Vircon32 emulator can run, or a BIOS.
.PP
Every path in the definition is relative to the directory the
definition file is in, not to the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output.v32"
Write the ROM to
.IR output.v32 .
Without
.BR \-o ,
the output path is the definition's path with its extension replaced
by
.IR .v32 .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose: report each step.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and author, and exit.
.SH ROM DEFINITION
.RS
.nf
<rom\-definition version="1.0">
    <rom type="cartridge" title="My Game" version="1.0" />
    <binary path="obj/game.vbin" />
    <textures>
        <texture path="obj/sprites.vtex" />
        <texture path="obj/background.vtex" />
    </textures>
    <sounds>
        <sound path="obj/music.vsnd" />
        <sound path="obj/jump.vsnd" />
    </sounds>
</rom\-definition>
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B <rom\-definition version>
The Vircon32 specification version the definition was written for,
as
.IR major.minor .
A version newer than the tools support is rejected.
.TP
.B <rom type>
.B cartridge
or
.BR bios .
.TP
.B <rom title>
Up to 63 characters, stored in the ROM header.
.TP
.B <rom version>
The game's own version, as
.IR major.minor .
.TP
.B <binary path>
The program, a VBIN file made by
.BR assemble (1).
.TP
.B <texture path>
A VTEX file made by
.BR png2vircon (1).
Textures get ids 0, 1, 2, ... in the order listed; a program selects
them by id. Up to 256 textures, each at most 1024 by 1024 pixels.
.TP
.B <sound path>
A VSND file made by
.BR wav2vircon (1).
Sounds get ids 0, 1, 2, ... in the order listed. Up to 1024 sounds,
each at most 268435456 samples long.
.PP
All four elements
.RB ( <rom> ", " <binary> ", " <textures> ", " <sounds> )
are required, but
.B <textures>
and
.B <sounds>
may be empty. A BIOS must contain exactly one texture (its font and
graphics, selectable as texture \-1 by programs) and one sound.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
A ROM file starts with a 128-byte header: the signature
.B V32\-CART
or
.BR V32\-BIOS ,
the Vircon32 version and revision, the title (64 bytes, zero-padded),
the ROM version and revision, the numbers of textures and sounds, and
the offset and length in bytes of the program, video and audio
sections. The three sections follow, holding the VBIN, VTEX and VSND
files as they were given (headers included). All numbers are
little-endian 32-bit integers.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The ROM was written.
.TP
.B 1
Any error: a missing element or attribute, a file that is not a valid
VBIN/VTEX/VSND, too many or too large textures or sounds, or a file
that can't be read or written. The message is printed as
.IR "packrom: error: description" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
packrom game.xml \-o bin/game.v32
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR assemble (1),
.BR png2vircon (1),
.BR wav2vircon (1),
.BR unpackrom (1),
.BR Vircon32 (1)
